# v3.0 - Changelog | Resources
created: 2023-06-22, last updated: 2026-03-13, [Read more](https://docs.geldata.com/resources/changelog/3_x)

### assert function ​
The new `assert` function lets you do handy things like create powerful
constraints when paired with triggers:
Copy
```
type Person {
required name: str;
multi friends: Person;
multi enemies: Person;
trigger prohibit_frenemies after insert, update for each do (
assert(
not exists (__new__.friends intersect __new__.enemies),
message := "Invalid frenemies",
)
)
}
```

# gel-js/docs/reference.rst at master · geldata/gel-js
created: 2015-09-13, last updated: 2026-04-17, [Read more](https://github.com/geldata/gel-js/blob/master/docs/reference.rst)

EdgeDB `array` maps onto the JavaScript `Array`.
```
// Use the Node.js assert library to test results.
const assert = require("assert");
const edgedb = require("edgedb");
async function main() {
const client = edgedb.createClient("edgedb://edgedb@localhost/");
const data = await client.querySingle("select [1, 2, 3]");
// The result is an Array.
assert(data instanceof Array);
assert(typeof data[0] === "number");
assert(data.length === 3);
assert(data[2] === 3);
}
main();

